        },
        "text": "In summary, our study results suggest that PD-1 inhibitors modify the composition of the gut microbiota in mice. The gut microbiota promotes PD-1 inhibitor-associated myocarditis by altering the number and function of Tregs. The gut microbiota may play an important role in potential therapeutic strategies to mitigate immune checkpoint inhibitor-associated cardiotoxicity."
